{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> I am trustworthy that you should believe in Me that I am able to do all these things — for I brought you out of the land of Egypt and performed for you great miracles." "<b>Pegs.</b> Like a peg at the two ends of the yoke, holding back the harness-band so it does not slip off the ox's head and loosen the binding — as in ״עֲשֵׂה לְךָ מוֹסֵרוֹת וּמֹטוֹת״ (Jeremiah 27); קַבִּילְיֵיא בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>Upright.</b> With an erect posture (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French cheville, 'peg/pin'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T17:26:21.048375295Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}